																		Thanks, Trivia, Explanation, and Other Matters
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/mrwrong" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2039383); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2039383&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607028383" alt="MrWrong" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2039383)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/mrwrong" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2039383); return false;" >MrWrong</a></span> <span class="odate time_1430187234 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">28 Apr 2015 02:13</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2280672">
									

<p>Firstly, allow me to thank all who had reviewed: Cimmerian, DreamwalkerFae, Leviathan34, Illustrio, NonPlusUltra and anyone whom I somehow missed out.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>To clarify, this is not El Dorado. El Dorado (the golden one) refers to a tribal chief who is said to cover himself in gold dust and dive into a lake.</p>
<p>This, however, is the following:</p>
<ul>
<li>Seven Cities of Gold</li>
<li>Cibola and Quivira</li>
<li>City of the Caesars</li>
<li>The golden city that was mislabelled as &quot;El Dorado&quot;</li>
<li>And every single &quot;lost city of gold&quot; in Latin America</li>
</ul>
<p>As to what is happening, SCP-2955 routinely &quot;moult&quot; gold nuggets which adds a surplus to Latin American gold. The Conquistadors decided to just grab everything that is made of gold, and SCP-2955 made a desperate attempt to escape them, hence its anomalous effect is simply a very drastic defence mechanism.</p>
<p>The last portion of the article was SCP-2955 deciding that the Foundation ultimately are &quot;good people&quot; like the natives were (as the Foundation opted to return the sample they took), in contrast to the &quot;bad people&quot; (i.e. the Conquistadors).</p>
</div>
</div>
