<p>I haven't add a nickname for the SCP on the mainlist yet. I will get to that when I pass the &quot;12-hour test&quot;.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-124877-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-124877-1')">1</a></sup></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><br />
As for the first question, I would say that the in-universe Foundation want to conceal the implications of the act. Said implication is that SCP-2955 <em>might</em> be sapient (as it somehow acknowledged the return of the lost pieces and showed some level of gratitude for the act), although it is hinted at the other addendum.</p>
<p>On the lower levels, it might be passed off as a &quot;sentient gold&quot; type of animal. On the higher levels, it would reveal the anomaly to be a race of &quot;sentient gold&quot; that actively interacted with humans (by providing native humans gold in exchange for providing them living space).</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>EDIT: Okay, you got a point and I've altered the last addendum as a result.</p>
